  "text": "Classic Neapolitan ice cream is a delightful combination of three flavors: vanilla, chocolate, and strawberry. Here's a simple recipe to make it at home:\n\n---\n\n**Classic Neapolitan Ice Cream Recipe**\n\n**Ingredients for 4 servings:**\n\n- 2 cups heavy cream\n- 1 cup whole milk\n- 3/4 cup sugar\n- 1 tbsp vanilla extract\n- 1/2 cup chocolate sauce (store-bought or homemade)\n- 1/2 cup strawberry puree (store-bought or homemade)\n- 1/2 cup whipped cream or whipped topping (optional, for garnish)\n- 1/2 cup chocolate shavings or chopped chocolate (optional, for garnish)\n\n---\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. **Make the base:**\n   - In a medium saucepan, combine the heavy cream, whole milk, and sugar.\n   - Heat over medium heat, stirring until the sugar dissolves.\n   - Remove from heat and stir in the vanilla extract.\n\n2. **Chill the base:**\n   - Let the mixture sit for about 10 minutes, then refrigerate for at least 30 minutes to chill.\n\n3. **Churn the ice cream:**\n   - Pour the chilled base into an ice cream maker and churn according to the manufacturer's instructions until it reaches a soft-serve consistency (usually about 20-30 minutes).\n\n4. **Fold in the flavors:**\n   - Once the base is ready, divide it into three equal parts.\n   - In one part, stir in the chocolate sauce.\n   - In another part, stir in the strawberry puree.\n   - The third part can be left plain vanilla (or you can double the vanilla in one portion if needed).\n\n5. **Freeze:**\n   - Transfer each flavored portion into separate containers or a large tub.\n   - Freeze for at least 4\u20136 hours, or until firm.\n\n6. **Serve:**\n   - Let the ice cream sit for 5\u201310 minutes before scooping.\n   - Garnish with whipped cream and chocolate shavings if desired.\n\n---\n\n**Tips:**\n- Use high-quality chocolate sauce and strawberry puree for the best flavor.\n- If you don\u2019t have an ice cream maker, you can pour the base into a\u5bc6\u5c01 container and freeze, stirring every 30 minutes to prevent ice crystals.\n\nEnjoy your homemade Neapolitan ice cream! \ud83c\udf66",
